# Compile-time code in a generic body that reads its type parameter's
# TypeInfo record runs once per instance: in `sizes`, a `#if` condition and a
# `name: #run value` local over `T.reflect()` give, for each type a call fills
# `T` with (directly or through `width_again`), the answer that type's record
# gives, on every tier. Two programs share `sizes` and fill `T` with
# different types; each computes its own answers, and `never_counted`, which
# no program calls, computes none and reports nothing.
fixture: AGenericBodyRunsCompileTimeCodePerInstance.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step o0: jet run -O0 wide.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "wide\n2\nnarrow\n0\nnarrow\n0\n"
step o1: jet run -O1 wide.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == o0
step o2: jet run -O2 wide.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == o0
step narrow0: jet run -O0 narrow.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "narrow\n1\nwide\n3\n"
step narrow2: jet run -O2 narrow.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == narrow0
